+SWC-TCF hands a monolithic mixed-integer program to a general-purpose
+solver: the two-commodity flow formulation of
+Sect.~\ref{sec:mpvrpp}, itself derived from the waste-collection model of
+Ramos et al.~\cite{RAMOS2018146} and the two-commodity device of Baldacci et
+al.~\cite{Baldacci2004TwoCommodity}, restated on directed arcs. The shipped
+model keeps one depot (the copy $n{+}1$ is folded away), places one arc
+binary $x_{ij}$ per ordered pair, priced at the directed kilometre $d_{ij}$
+actually driven, and carries the two commodities as separate arc flows: $f$
+(the load) and $h$ (the residual capacity), coupled by
+$f_{ij} + h_{ij} = Q\,x_{ij}$. Flow conservation at the bins, not the
+coupling alone, is what eliminates sub-tours; disconnected cycles of
+zero-demand bins are excluded by the degree constraints. The visit binary
+$g_i$ is first-class, so the objective $R \sum_i w_i g_i - C \sum_{i,j}
+d_{ij} x_{ij} - \Omega k$ trades revenue against travel and a per-vehicle
+charge directly, with no retrofit beyond the profitable-subset objective.
+
+Two adaptations matter for reproduction. First, the source model's
+overflow-count constraint is not implemented: the service level enters
+through the bins released by mandatory selection, and every bin whose sensed
+fill reaches $\psi E_i$ is forced ($g_i = 1$); in the reported configurations
+$\psi = 1$, so only full bins are forced beyond the mandatory set, and if the
+forced set itself is infeasible for the fleet the solver retries once
+without forcing. Second, the model is solved in percent of bin capacity, with
+revenue and payload rescaled accordingly, and arcs longer than
+$6{,}000$\,km are dropped before solving. The saved configurations use the
+native Gurobi backend with a 60\,s time limit, a $1\%$ MIP gap, and
+$\Omega = 0.1$\,€ per vehicle inside the optimisation; the benchmark's
+reported profit carries no per-vehicle term ($\Omega = 0$ in the accounting
+of Sect.~\ref{sec:protocol}). On a timeout the solver returns its best
+incumbent.
+
+Its main limitation is scale. The model grows with the square of the
+candidate bins and there is no decomposition to keep the working problem
+small, making it the constructor most vulnerable to instance-size blow-up.
+The largest scenario exhibits this vulnerability
 (Sect.~\ref{sec:integrity}).
 
